Worldview's two scores and its treatment of integrity and the created future
come from the ontological leadership model of Werner Erhard, Michael C. Jensen,
Steve Zaffron, and Kari Granger:

  Being a Leader and the Effective Exercise of Leadership
  https://papers.ssrn.com/sol3/papers.cfm?abstract_id=1263835

  Integrity: A Positive Model that Incorporates the Normative Phenomena of
  Morality, Ethics, and Legality
  https://papers.ssrn.com/sol3/papers.cfm?abstract_id=1542759

Specifically: integrity as a positive rather than normative phenomenon, the
cascade from integrity to workability to performance, the six components of
one's word, the distinction between keeping and honoring one's word, and the
future as a context one lives into rather than a prediction.

This repository is an original implementation informed by those papers. It is
not endorsed by their authors, does not reproduce them, and is not a substitute
for reading them.
